    \field{abstract}{%
    Given a pair of \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{W\}{\textasciicircum}*\$-algebras \$({\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\},{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{R\})\$ with \$({\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\})\_*\$ separable, a measurable space \$(Σ, {\textbackslash}mathcal\{F\})\$ and a POVM \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}: {\textbackslash}mathcal\{F\} {\textbackslash}to {\textbackslash}mathcal\{E\}({\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{R\})\$, the integral of a function \$f: Σ{\textbackslash}to {\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\}\$ is defined as an element of the spatial tensor product \${\textbackslash}int f {\textbackslash}otimes d{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\} {\textbackslash}in {\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\} {\textbackslash}bar\{{\textbackslash}otimes\} {\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{R\}\$. The space
  \$B\_b(Σ,{\textbackslash}mathcal\{F\},{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\})\$ of uniformly bounded ultraweakly measurable functions is the universal domain of integration; once \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}\$ is fixed it refines to the quotient \$L{\textasciicircum}{\textbackslash}infty\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}(Σ,{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\}) = B\_b(Σ,{\textbackslash}mathcal\{F\},{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\})/{\textbackslash}mathcal\{N\}\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}\$ by \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}\$-null functions. When \$({\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{R\})\_*\$ is also separable, \$L{\textasciicircum}{\textbackslash}infty\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}(Σ,{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\}) {\textbackslash}cong {\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\} {\textbackslash}bar\{{\textbackslash}otimes\}
  L{\textasciicircum}{\textbackslash}infty\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}(Σ)\$ is a \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{W\}{\textasciicircum}*\$-algebra. The integration map is a faithful normal unital completely positive (CP) map, a \$*\$-homomorphism for PVMs and an isometry for localizable POVMs. It can be identified with the spatial tensor product \${\textbackslash}boldsymbol\{1\}\_\{{\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{S\}\} {\textbackslash}hat\{{\textbackslash}otimes\} Φ\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}\$ where \$Φ\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}: L{\textasciicircum}{\textbackslash}infty\_{\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}(Σ) {\textbackslash}to {\textbackslash}mathcal\{M\}\_{\textbackslash}mathcal\{R\}\$ is the faithful normal positive map corresponding to \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{E\}\$. Complete positivity of integration maps is derived from Stinespring factorization through Naimark dilation. We establish an operator-valued Leibniz rule and Fubini theorem.%
